fix(test): update the harnesses the served route map changed

Three CI jobs failed on the manifest change, each correctly.

test_cli_http_transport.c asserted specific method -> path mappings. That
is the SERVER's property now; asserting it in a client unit test would
re-create the second copy this removed, and it is already covered where
the map lives (server-api-conformance-check, the route descriptor). The
test now installs a synthetic manifest and covers what IS still the
client's: the sync/async split, the verb, and unknown methods resolving to
nothing. cli_v1_manifest_set_for_test() is the seam — in-process only,
called from tests, never a way around the fetch.

test_cli_v1_delegate.c links the HTTP transport now, because
cli_v1_route_for_method calls through it even when no server answers. Its
own aimee_home stub means aimee_home.o must stay out of that link line.
(Its route assertions still pass unchanged: doctor.forensics, kb.health
and kb.ingest.status resolve through bespoke[], which is consulted before
the manifest.)

test-thin-client-remote-exclusive.py stands up a stand-in server that
answered every path with one canned body. The client now asks that server
what it routes before routing anything, so the stub has to answer
/v1/cli/manifest too; without it every command failed before the request
under test was made. Only the methods this test drives need rows.

cli_v1_async_route_for_method gains a header declaration — it had none and
lived TU-locally, which is why the rewritten test could not call it.

The proposal is corrected on a point I got wrong: command_registry.h reads
as though every surface already routes from it, and I cited it that way.
Measured: aimee_command_register is called only from its own tests, so the
registry is empty at runtime and its one production reader iterates
nothing. It is a correct design with no data in it, and that matters for
phasing — it cannot be the thing definitions are served from until
something populates it.

Verified locally: unit-test-cli-http-transport, unit-test-cli-v1-delegate,
test-thin-client-remote-exclusive, and the CI skill-lint step reproduced
in a temp HOME (12 skills passed) all pass.
